From 34a2bb644cf82538caaf01784253c5ff3fd46b79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 20:34:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] service/notifications: forward Wayland activation tokens
 when invoking actions

NotificationAction.invoke() requests an xdg-activation token for the
input that invoked it and sends the server's ActivationToken signal with
it before ActionInvoked, as the Desktop Notifications spec allows, so the
client can activate its window. Without Wayland or a token, only
ActionInvoked is sent, as before. A test checks the order.
